{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-matthew-015",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 15,
  "title": "Matthew 15",
  "display_title": "Matthew 15",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "matthew",
  "book": "Matthew",
  "bookName": "Matthew",
  "bookOrder": 40,
  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 15,
  "sortOrder": 40015,
  "verseCount": 39,
  "aliases": [
    "Matt",
    "Mt"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Then came to Jesus scribes and Pharisees, which were of Jerusalem, saying,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Why do thy disciples transgress the tradition of the elders? for they wash not their hands when they eat bread.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "But he answered and said unto them, Why do ye also transgress the commandment of God by your tradition?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "For God commanded, saying, Honour thy father and mother: and, He that curseth father or mother, let him die the death.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "But ye say, Whosoever shall say to his father or his mother, It is a gift, by whatsoever thou mightest be profited by me;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "And honour not his father or his mother, he shall be free. Thus have ye made the commandment of God of none effect by your tradition.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Ye hypocrites, well did Esaias prophesy of you, saying,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "This people draweth nigh unto me with their mouth, and honoureth me with their lips; but their heart is far from me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "But in vain they do worship me, teaching for doctrines the commandments of men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "And he called the multitude, and said unto them, Hear, and understand:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Not that which goeth into the mouth defileth a man; but that which cometh out of the mouth, this defileth a man.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Then came his disciples, and said unto him, Knowest thou that the Pharisees were offended, after they heard this saying?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "But he answered and said, Every plant, which my heavenly Father hath not planted, shall be rooted up.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Let them alone: they be blind leaders of the blind. And if the blind lead the blind, both shall fall into the ditch.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Then answered Peter and said unto him, Declare unto us this parable.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "And Jesus said, Are ye also yet without understanding?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "Do not ye yet understand, that whatsoever entereth in at the mouth goeth into the belly, and is cast out into the draught?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "But those things which proceed out of the mouth come forth from the heart; and they defile the man.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "For out of the heart proceed evil thoughts, murders, adulteries, fornications, thefts, false witness, blasphemies:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "These are the things which defile a man: but to eat with unwashen hands defileth not a man.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Then Jesus went thence, and departed into the coasts of Tyre and Sidon.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "And, behold, a woman of Canaan came out of the same coasts, and cried unto him, saying, Have mercy on me, O Lord, thou son of David; my daughter is grievously vexed with a devil.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "But he answered her not a word. And his disciples came and besought him, saying, Send her away; for she crieth after us.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "But he answered and said, I am not sent but unto the lost sheep of the house of Israel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "Then came she and worshipped him, saying, Lord, help me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "But he answered and said, It is not meet to take the children’s bread, and to cast it to dogs.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "And she said, Truth, Lord: yet the dogs eat of the crumbs which fall from their masters’ table.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "Then Jesus answered and said unto her, O woman, great is thy faith: be it unto thee even as thou wilt. And her daughter was made whole from that very hour.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "And Jesus departed from thence, and came nigh unto the sea of Galilee; and went up into a mountain, and sat down there.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "And great multitudes came unto him, having with them those that were lame, blind, dumb, maimed, and many others, and cast them down at Jesus’ feet; and he healed them:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "Insomuch that the multitude wondered, when they saw the dumb to speak, the maimed to be whole, the lame to walk, and the blind to see: and they glorified the God of Israel.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "Then Jesus called his disciples unto him, and said, I have compassion on the multitude, because they continue with me now three days, and have nothing to eat: and I will not send them away fasting, lest they faint in the way.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "And his disciples say unto him, Whence should we have so much bread in the wilderness, as to fill so great a multitude?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:33"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-034",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 34,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:34",
      "numberLabel": "34",
      "text": "And Jesus saith unto them, How many loaves have ye? And they said, Seven, and a few little fishes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:34",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:34"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-035",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 35,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:35",
      "numberLabel": "35",
      "text": "And he commanded the multitude to sit down on the ground.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:35",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:35"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-036",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 36,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:36",
      "numberLabel": "36",
      "text": "And he took the seven loaves and the fishes, and gave thanks, and brake them, and gave to his disciples, and the disciples to the multitude.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:36",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:36"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-037",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 37,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:37",
      "numberLabel": "37",
      "text": "And they did all eat, and were filled: and they took up of the broken meat that was left seven baskets full.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:37",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:37"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-038",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 38,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:38",
      "numberLabel": "38",
      "text": "And they that did eat were four thousand men, beside women and children.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:38",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:38"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-039",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 39,
      "verseId": "kjv:matthew:15:39",
      "numberLabel": "39",
      "text": "And he sent away the multitude, and took ship, and came into the coasts of Magdala.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Matthew 15:39",
        "verseKey": "kjv:matthew:15:39"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
